2025-05-01 00:45:22 - Thread-9 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns & possible conditions  

• "country_code": filter to U.S. patents ( "country_code" = 'US' ).  
• "kind_code": keep only B‑series grants ( "kind_code" = 'B2' ).  
• "application_kind": utility patents are usually coded ‘A’; keep only those ( "application_kind" = 'A' ).  
• "grant_date": keep grants issued 20220601 – 20220831 (numeric yyyymmdd).  
• "ipc": Variant array that holds IPC objects; flatten it to read the field `"code"`.  
• "publication_number": handy identifier for inspection / grouping.  

------------------------------------------------------------------
Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to the aggregation needed to discover the most‑frequent 4‑digit IPC code for U.S. B2 utility patents granted June–August 2022.  
(Replace PATENTS.PATENTS with the correct database & schema names only if they differ.)

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at 20 U.S. B2 publications granted between 1 Jun and 31 Aug 2022
SELECT 
  "publication_number",
  "grant_date",
  "kind_code",
  "application_kind",
  "country_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Check which kind codes appear in that date‑range to verify we’re really seeing only B2
SELECT DISTINCT "kind_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Inspect distinct application kinds in the same slice; we expect mainly 'A'
SELECT DISTINCT "application_kind"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS
WHERE "country_code" = 'US'
  AND "kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND "grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Show raw IPC JSON objects for a few sample patents in the cohort
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  ipc_item.value AS "ipc_raw"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Extract full IPC code strings for those patents
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING AS "ipc_code"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Derive 4‑digit IPC (first four characters) and list 20 examples
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  SUBSTR(ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count occurrences of each 4‑digit IPC (still limited to show any 20 counts)
SELECT 
  SUBSTR(ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
  COUNT(*) AS "n_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
GROUP BY "ipc4"
ORDER BY "n_pub" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Same as #7 but keeping only the main IPCs (when field "first" = TRUE, if present)
SELECT 
  SUBSTR(ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "ipc4",
  COUNT(*) AS "n_pub"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
  AND COALESCE(ipc_item.value:"first"::BOOLEAN, FALSE) = TRUE
GROUP BY "ipc4"
ORDER BY "n_pub" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Show which publication numbers contribute to the single most frequent 4‑digit IPC
WITH top_ipc AS (
  SELECT 
    SUBSTR(ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS ipc4,
    COUNT(*) AS n_pub
  FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item
  WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
    AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
    AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
    AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
  GROUP BY ipc4
  ORDER BY n_pub DESC
  LIMIT 1
)
SELECT 
  p."publication_number",
  SUBSTR(ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "top_ipc4"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item,
     top_ipc
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
  AND SUBSTR(ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) = top_ipc.ipc4
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final aggregation to reveal the single most common 4‑digit IPC code
SELECT 
  SUBSTR(ipc_item.value:"code"::STRING, 1, 4) AS "most_common_ipc4",
  COUNT(*) AS "publications_with_ipc4"
FROM PATENTS.PATENTS.PUBLICATIONS p,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => p."ipc") ipc_item
WHERE p."country_code" = 'US'
  AND p."kind_code" = 'B2'
  AND p."application_kind" = 'A'
  AND p."grant_date" BETWEEN 20220601 AND 20220831
GROUP BY "most_common_ipc4"
ORDER BY "publications_with_ipc4" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

Run the final query (#10) without the `LIMIT` or with `LIMIT 1` to obtain the single most frequent 4‑digit IPC code for U.S. B2 utility patents granted in June–August 2022.
